; BOUNCE BONANZA - TIME'S UP (SPEC.md 130.22.9.1): the timeout's tune, played
; over the finish sequence's 2 s (BZ_FIN_STEPS = 110 sub-ticks) in the course
; song's place, as the VICTORY fanfare is on a goal.  A minor at 164 BPM - a
; 16th is a row of FIVE sub-ticks - two patterns of 11 rows, exactly 110
; sub-ticks of sound:
;   A  the horn falls by semitones: G, F#, F - the "wah, wah, wah"
;   B  ...and lands on a long E over A minor's dominant, sagging to silence
; and a third pattern of nothing, which `loop` points at: the song does NOT
; repeat, it ends in silence (victory.bmu's shape).
; On the speaker the lead is the whole tune (the bass only where it rests).

song timeup "Time's Up"
groove 5
unit 16
rows 11
spkbass
voice lead horn
voice bass bass
voice chord strings

lead LA = o4 v14 g4 f+4 f8. |
lead LB = o4 v14 e2 v10 e16 r8 |
bass BA = o3 l16 c:4 c:4 b:3 |
bass BB = o2 l16 a:8 r:3 |
chord CA = o3 [e g >c]:4 [d+ f+ a]:4 [d f b]:3 |
chord CB = o3 [e g+ b]:8 r:3 |
drum DA = l16 t r r r t r r r t r r |
drum DB = l16 k:8 r:3 |

order LA BA CA DA
order LB BB CB DB
order - - - -
loop 2
